# validate-vendors order-dependent corpus — RED observations (pre-fix)

This failure is intermittent and load-sensitive, so the raw runs are recorded as observations
rather than one clean repro. All three observations are from the pre-fix tree.

## 1) Exact 5-file order (2026-11-01 14:20 local)
command: corepack pnpm exec vitest run test/s594-r30-evidence-fence.test.ts test/run101-r2-public-queue-store.test.ts test/run101-r5-cancel-drain.test.ts test/run101-r9-queue-operator-proxy.test.ts test/validate-vendors.test.ts
result: exit 1 — 1 failed | 21 passed (22)
failure: Corpus case craft.chat.non-tool-mentions-tools.005 produced execution family vendor-litellm instead of vendor-llama-swap.

## 2) s594 + validate only (2026-11-01 15:32 local)
command: corepack pnpm exec vitest run test/s594-r30-evidence-fence.test.ts test/validate-vendors.test.ts
result: exit 1 — 1 failed | 9 passed (10)
failure: Corpus case pi.responses.alias-easy-001 produced execution family remote-service instead of vendor-llama-swap
  (endpoint=openai.personal.openai-codex-subscription.global.gpt-5.4, model=chatgpt/gpt-5.4,
  vendor=chatgpt-codex-responses, adapter=codex-subscription-responses)
diagnostics: cacheContinuity.activeEndpointId=codex; difficultyRouting.strategy=cost;
  observedProfile.source=runtime-state; observedProfile.readMode=per-request.

## 3) Pairwise/process isolation used for diagnosis
- s594 direct fence-store tests + validate: 2/2 pass in each of 2 attempts.
- s594 integration-only tests + validate: 2/2 pass in each of 2 attempts.
- s594 and validate in separate vitest processes: pass.
- s594 + validate in one process: failed in 1 of the first attempts.
This places the trigger in process-local runtime state/timing, not in the queue rows, temp dirs,
kill switches, or environment variables (the queue tests mutate none of those).

## Root cause
The queue suites change elapsed time/scheduling enough for the hybrid runtime's observed endpoint
profiles (written by warmups and earlier corpus cases) to become visible to later corpus requests.
The validation plan already disables observed learning for corpus routing, but
readObservedProfilesForRouting ignored observed_data.enabled and still read live profiles, so the
cost strategy could select the remote/Codex endpoint for a case whose expected family is local.
Waiting for the codex endpoint or disabling observed data on the corpus-only config removes the
race; the second validation test still exercises observed-profile diagnostics because it uses a
config with observed data enabled.
